        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was likely caused by the removal of the `reloadText()` method in the command classes, which was responsible for updating the help text. Without this method, the help text may not have been properly initialized or updated, leading to incorrect or missing help information when the `/help` command was invoked. The changes to the `CommandParser` class, which removed the bulk reloading of command help text, further exacerbated this issue by preventing any updates to the help text when commands were parsed.

        Commit message:
        fixed /help bug introduced by cfbce4351327f0f1a52a  

        Patch:
        diff --git a/src/simpleserver/CommandParser.java b/src/simpleserver/CommandParser.java
index 59b6694..42cfffa 100644
--- a/src/simpleserver/CommandParser.java
+++ b/src/simpleserver/CommandParser.java
